{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/62150-fourth-faction-of-werewolves-neither-forsaken-pure-nor-bale-hound","id":62150,"title":"Fourth Faction of Werewolves - Neither Forsaken, Pure Nor Bale Hound","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-31T07:22:51-08:00","id":62150,"title":"Fourth Faction of Werewolves - Neither Forsaken, Pure Nor Bale Hound","content":"So I was thinking over the possible Ghost Wolf-born tribes in <i>The Rage</i>, and it got me thinking of how these tribes might fall into the political landscape of <i>Werewolf: the Forsaken</i>. From what I have read, they are presented as options for the Forsaken side of things, but I had a more interesting idea: they fall onto neither existing side. These three tribes (I believe there are three, please correct me if I am wrong), if used in a game, could potentially shake things up by neither identifying with the Forsaken or the Pure.<br /> <br /> How might this be possible?<br /> <br /> The three new tribes do not like the politics of either faction, seeing them as extremes. They aim to adopt a centrist position among the tribes, neither pro- nor anti-Luna in full, but leaning a little to either side. They are also divided on Shadow-Policing vs. Shadow-Serving, and whether or not Pangaea is a good or a bad thing for the modern world. Here's how I imagine things:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Tower Hounds </i></b><i>(Anzaghar Ilthum): </i>The Tower Hounds are presented as a secret police, the &quot;watchers who watch the watchdog&quot;. This, in my mind, makes them a &quot;beta&quot; pack to the &quot;alpha&quot; back of the Speakers of the Vine, who are presented as diplomats (see below). They are the most neutral towards the Pure and the Forsaken, as everyone needs someone to call out their bullcrap, but believe in the Forsaken stance of policing the Shadow. Father Wolf was the watchdog against the spirits, after all, and it is only proper that werewolves keep a lid on things. Why let things like Hosts and <i>magath </i>run rampant when there are more important things to do? And, as an extension of that, they are neutral on Pangaea; their problem is the immediate now, not things mythical and long-gone.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Speakers of the Vine </i></b><i>(Khuranu Dhugu): </i>The Speakers of the Vine are, by oath, diplomats and arbitrators before anything else. They are the alphas of this third faction, as they take a leadership stance not unlike the Storm Lords' \u2014 that said, the Speakers see showing weakness as acceptance that one is imperfect. They lean towards the Pure because they see wisdom and fair points in their beliefs and arguments; towards the Shadow, they are neutral on whether it is policed or pandered to. In their minds, anyone can be reasoned with, and diplomacy in the Shadow is similar to diplomacy among werewolves. That being said, they feel Pangaea would be a <i>very bad idea </i>to bring back, as the balance of the world is already upset and needing fixing.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Savage Priests</i></b><i> (Idimathu): </i>The Savage Priests are a reflection of the Fire-Touched among the Pure. Like the Fire-Touched, they accept new converts into the Forsaken fold with open arms \u2014 and, on occasion, some well-hidden silver. Their very nature and tribal oath leans them towards the Forsaken, as they see the Pure misguided and hurt from wounds that are millenniums old. Their views on the Shadow might seem odd \u2014 why would Father Wolf's own priests want to serve that which he had to control? \u2014 but there are many powerful allies in the Shadow. It takes a few honeyed words and dollops of promised Essence, but the Savage Priests have turned many of the Pure's allies to their side. They very much would like a return of Pangaea, as it is was their Father's paradise.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Ghost Wolves</b>: </i>The Forsaken often look upon Ghost Wolves with disrespect or pity. The Pure outright loathe them and refer to them as &quot;half-wolves&quot;. This third faction, however? Being born from the aspirations of Ghost Wolves who did not fit in, Ghost Wolves are accepted or outright embraced. If the Forsaken are a middle-ground and the Pure a hateful extreme, then the views on Ghost Wolves are extremely idealistic in this faction. Even the Savage Priests will leave Ghost Wolves alone, on the basis of, &quot;A Ghost Wolf without brands is neither Pure nor Forsaken, and a Ghost Wolf with their brands is already Forsaken by nature.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><b>Bale Hounds</b>: </i>Still universally reviled. You will be hard-pressed to find wolves in this third faction that believe any of these can be redeemed. The Speakers do not trust their words or motives, the Tower Hounds want to kill every one of them for being complete monsters, and the Priests consider them heretics that should be scoured by silver and burned at the stake.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 01-31-2014, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T07:31:55-08:00","id":62155,"title":"","content":"It seems like they were spawned by the Bale Hounds of Beliar, the Maeljin of Sloth. In not picking sides, not choosing something to go for, they'd be stalling the activities of both sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T07:38:20-08:00","id":62158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/62150-fourth-faction-of-werewolves-neither-forsaken-pure-nor-bale-hound?p=62155#post62155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like they were spawned by the Bale Hounds of Beliar, the Maeljin of Sloth. In not picking sides, not choosing something to go for, they'd be stalling the activities of both sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how would Beliar influence them if they are anti-Bale Hound and continue the upkeep of the Shadow, but do so in their own ways? Bale Hounds embedded deep in the tribal structure, subtly turning things their way?<br /> <br /> One could also say Soulless-Wolf had foul, corrupted progeny of his own masquerading as totems. Ramamu-Ur could be his son, and Crown-On-the-Tower a spy; Wind In the Wolf's Lair could be a subtle, corrupting presence that erodes, based on where Crow-On-the-Tower says the best place to start trouble and plant sloth is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T07:49:10-08:00","id":62162,"title":"","content":"You wouldn't have to have Bale Hounds active within, it just sounds like the idea may have been started by Bale Hounds, or likely Beliar, who promote inaction and apathy.<br /> If these tribes managed to get Uratha to convert to them (and make it at least an accepted practice), and maintain a much more on the fence stand of things, even if they hated the Bale Hounds or Maeljin, it wouldn't matter, cause they'd have already won. Bale Hounds of Sloth are wicked dudes, they view the heat death of the universe as the ultimate win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T08:12:11-08:00","id":62178,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just how I see the Forsaken/Pure split (basically, a family argument), but I don't see that a &quot;neutral party&quot; brings anything to the table and it doesn't really make sense as it's a family feud. Brother against brother (or, really distant cousins against distant cousins, but whatever) doesn't really end up with a neutral party except the parents, and Father Wolf is gone and Mother Luna is staying out of it. The siblings rarely stay neutral, maybe someone will try to keep the peace and <i>claim </i>to be neutral, but when part of the family isn't around, they make it clear which side they are on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T08:17:10-08:00","id":62186,"title":"","content":"@Papa Bear: Could you say, then, that when the chips are down, it's very likely the Tower Hounds will become amoral mercs going at either side, the Speakers will probably join the Pure and act as the &quot;face of the band&quot;, and the Savage Priests will go murder-crazy on any Pure or Pure sympathizers?<br /> <br /> @nofather: I really need to re-read <i>Blasphemies</i>, I've completely forgotten about that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:28:31-08:00","id":62236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/62150-fourth-faction-of-werewolves-neither-forsaken-pure-nor-bale-hound?p=62186#post62186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@nofather: I really need to re-read <i>Blasphemies</i>, I've completely forgotten about that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's really one of my favorite Werewolf books.<br /> I feel like I should point out I don't think your idea is bad. A lot of people seem to want to get away from the tribes as they are, if the 'what would you like about idigam chronicles' is any indication, so if your group has been looking for something this may be it. I was just offering a suggestion.<br /> <br /> In my own games, though I'm not running Werewolf now, Soulless Wolf has his own tribe, and while not quite a slave of the maeljin, he exists with a 'do what thou wilt' mentality, with some aggression towards the other tribes. The Bale Hounds of the Maeljin also exist, however, pretty much as Blasphemies has it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:32:59-08:00","id":62240,"title":"","content":"Theres a few hooks for new tribes within some of the books. Tribes of the moon mentions that Fenris had a brother wolf, a &quot;creator&quot; that might have gone mad with grief or some such when father wolf was killed and split off from the rest of the pack, never to be seen again. The hook itself says he might have his own tribe of werewolves moving for their own ends in Urfahra's memory.<br /> <br /> Nofather- It warms my angry angry heart to see someone using the soulless wolf as the 9th tribe concept. In my opinion the bale hounds work better as villains that have a purpose, then villains who just happen to be evil because they liked to party in vegas way to much. The 9th tribe gives them a focus. &gt;.&gt; I might also argue they're better than black spirals as the nature doesn't completely consume them, at least until they become broken souls. Sucks for bale hounds of violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 01-31-2014, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:09:50-08:00","id":62274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/62150-fourth-faction-of-werewolves-neither-forsaken-pure-nor-bale-hound?p=62186#post62186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Papa Bear: Could you say, then, that when the chips are down, it's very likely the Tower Hounds will become amoral mercs going at either side, the Speakers will probably join the Pure and act as the &quot;face of the band&quot;, and the Savage Priests will go murder-crazy on any Pure or Pure sympathizers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it looks to me like all three of the Tribes you have there would side with The Pure if pushed because they are either taking a sympathetic view of the Shadow creatures or The Pure to begin with (Speakers of the Vine and Savage Priests) or tend to fall in with the others like younger siblings (Tower Hounds).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:51:15-08:00","id":64030,"title":"","content":"You know you could go with a children of gaia concept going with the Creator Wolf mythos. One that finds the other Tribes completely culpable for the death of Urfahra, including the Pure as they did nothing to stop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T08:46:07-08:00","id":81610,"title":"","content":"@Nofather: Your suggestions are completely welcome! No good can come of something without a little critique on its rough draft. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Papa Bear: That could be a plot hook for these three. Suggestions for making them swing towards the Forsaken side might include harsher policies on the Shadow and Pure, and their current states are bound to disturb a number of Uratha.<br /> <br /> @Lyrics of War: That is an absolutely brilliant idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}